<section image-layout="blank" id="BEYU4ODIlj" vertical-align="top"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ia5gtTPcKs"><p role="eyebrow">Era 03 · Generated variation</p><h2>Computational intelligence makes the output variable</h2><p font-size="18pt">The designer increasingly specifies a space of possible outputs rather than one resolved artifact.</p><grid marker="number" marker-size="large" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="chevron" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-fill="true" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="1em" style="--marker-chip-padding: 0.75em;"><grid-item id="VOnaVbBZGp" colspan="10"><h4>Intent + constraints</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="S7U2uUrte1" colspan="10"><h4>Data, rules, or prompt</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="UpPqT2yWeK" colspan="10"><h4>Model computation</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="EhpUD1aREZ" colspan="10"><h4>Output</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="0xdrqIVHgq" colspan="10"><h4>Human judgment</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="x_7A7K2-X7" colspan="10"><h4>Revise ↺</h4></grid-item></grid><p font-size="18pt"><b>The loop closes:</b> evaluation updates the next constraints; the system is iterative, not autonomous.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="dCQjsPlGmU" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow"><span text-color="#30363A">What scales</span></p><h3>Variation and adaptation</h3><p font-size="16pt">Repeated synthesis can respond to many contexts.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="n6WvFgZCVM" background-color="accent" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">What becomes design work</p><h3>Conditions for judgment</h3><p font-size="16pt">Provenance, opacity, bias, evaluation, and responsible revision.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>